cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you build on this idea or these results, please cite it as below."
title: "Is It Really Forgotten? Occupancy Models for Auditing LLM Unlearning (a pre-registered negative result)"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Kansal
    given-names: Parit
    website: "https://paritkansal.in"
repository-code: "https://github.com/ParitKansal/llm-unlearning-occupancy-audit"
url: "https://github.com/ParitKansal/llm-unlearning-occupancy-audit"
date-released: 2026-10-05
version: "1.0.0"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Tests whether ecological occupancy models, which separate presence from imperfect detection, can estimate how much
  "unlearned" knowledge an LLM still stores, using repeated heterogeneous probes. A pre-registered kill experiment on
  TOFU with public Llama-3.2-1B unlearning checkpoints (GradDiff, NPO, RMU) found that single-probe metrics undercount
  stored knowledge by 1.6-3.4x and that the occupancy estimate matched a relearning ground truth for GradDiff and NPO,
  but failed the never-trained control (clustered false positives on guessable facts) and missed knowledge that RMU
  hides from all black-box probes. Verdict: NO-GO.
keywords:
  - machine unlearning
  - large language models
  - unlearning evaluation
  - occupancy models
  - imperfect detection
  - negative result
  - pre-registration
